      "side": 1,
      "message": "How about defining a macro NUM_KEYSLOTS() so that this off-by-one quirk gets handled in one place, not 5 places?\n\n /*\n * The actual number of configurations supported is (CFGC+1), so slot numbers\n  * range from 0 to config_count inclusive.\n  */\n #define NUM_KEYSLOTS(hba)      (hba-\u003ecrypto_capabilities.config_count + 1)\n\ni.e. also use this when iterating \u0027slot \u003d 0; slot \u003c NUM_KEYSLOTS(hba); slot++\u0027, and when allocating stuff in ufshcd_hba_init_crypto().  Currently those both have to take into account the \"the hardware is off by one\" quirk, which is error-prone.",
